runs/live/

# The heavy two thirds of a run directory. Neither of these is read by a later
# generation or by the reader - `docs/design.md`, "What a later run needs from an
# earlier one", says which files are - and both outgrew git. A rollout dump with
# traces is roughly three times the same dump without them (28.5 MB becomes 9.3),
# and when crypto's held-out set went from 30 days to 120 the candidate dump hit
# 102.54 MB, which GitHub refuses. Three scheduled runs on 25 and 26 September
# reached a verdict, published it, and then could not push the generation that
# produced it; `rsi-arena next` could not see gen8 and the lineage restarted from
# gen7.
#
# Their durable home is S3 (`s3://$TRACE_BUCKET/rsi-arena/<topic>/<run>/`, synced
# before the commit step so the evidence survives a commit that fails) and, for a
# fortnight, the per-run artifact. `scripts/fetch_run.py` brings either back.
#
# `runs/**/gepa/` also covers the 2,600-file generated_best_outputs_valset tree
# this rule used to name on its own - and covers it at every depth, which the old
# `runs/*/gepa/...` did not: every topic writes to `runs/<topic>/<gen>/gepa/`, so
# 26,995 of those files were tracked anyway.
runs/**/rollouts/
runs/**/gepa/

# Agent worktrees and local Claude state
.claude/
